## Typical failure modes and the right fix

| Failure pattern | Root cause | Fix op |
|-----------------|------------|--------|
| Cherry-pick conflict on `file X` between commit `A` in milestone M1 and commit `B` in milestone M2, where `A` really needs `B` to land first | Missing DAG edge | `add_edge {source: M2, target: M1}` |
| Commit `C` in milestone M1 fails to cherry-pick because it touches code that was added by commit `D`, where `D` is in milestone M2 and was placed there by mistake | Commit placement | `move_commit {sha: D, from: M2, to: M1}` |
| Cherry-pick conflict caused by a pure-whitespace / rename-only commit | Noise commit | `drop_commit {sha, milestone}` |
| Same commit appears in two milestones (duplicate) | CSV error | `drop_commit` from the wrong one |
| Milestone has zero-length or all-broken commits after repeated retries | Unfixable milestone | `drop_milestone {id}` (last resort) |

Prefer the smallest intervention. Order by priority: `add_edge` → `move_commit` → `drop_commit` → `drop_milestone`.

