## Op schema (strict)

```json
{
  "ops": [
    {
      "op": "add_edge",
      "source_id": "M_foo",
      "target_id": "M_bar",
      "rationale": "Cherry-pick of 83a9c1 into M_bar fails on handler.py; the BaseHandler class it uses was added by commit 4ea230 in M_foo."
    },
    {
      "op": "move_commit",
      "commit_sha": "4ea230de",
      "from_milestone_id": "M_misc",
      "to_milestone_id": "M_foo",
      "rationale": "4ea230 introduces BaseHandler which M_foo depends on; wrongly grouped under M_misc."
    }
  ]
}
```

Supported ops (Phase A):

- `add_edge` — `{source_id, target_id, rationale}`
- `remove_edge` — `{source_id, target_id, rationale}`
- `move_commit` — `{commit_sha, from_milestone_id, to_milestone_id, rationale}`
- `drop_commit` — `{commit_sha, milestone_id, rationale}`
- `drop_milestone` — `{id, rationale}`

Every op **must** include `rationale` — it gets persisted to `stage1_fix_log.json` and reviewed by the Main Agent later.

